.TH MU2EDAQ-TOOLS 1 "2026-07-27" "mu2edaq-commandline-tools 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq-tools \- command line utilities for the Mu2e DAQ suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq-tools
.RI [ global-options ]
.I command
.RI [ command-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2edaq-tools
is the dispatcher for the Mu2e DAQ command line utilities. Each utility is a
subcommand; run
.B mu2edaq-tools list
to see the ones this build provides.
.PP
Configuration is resolved from four sources. Highest precedence first:
command line options, environment variables
.RB ( MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_ *),
the YAML config file, and the built-in defaults. None of them are required:
with no config file and an empty environment the defaults are a usable
configuration.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List the available tools with their one-line descriptions.
.TP
.B config " [--json]"
Show the effective configuration and the config file it came from. With
.B --json
the output is a JSON object with
.I config_file
and
.I values
members, suitable for scripting.
.TP
.B version
Print the package version.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Read configuration from
.I FILE
instead of searching the standard locations.
.TP
.BR \-\-cluster " \fINAME\fR"
Cluster to operate on. Default:
.BR mu2edaq .
.TP
.BR \-\-discovery\-timeout " \fISECONDS\fR"
Seconds to wait for mu2edaq-discovery responses. Default:
.BR 2.0 .
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level " \fILEVEL\fR"
One of DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR, CRITICAL. Default:
.BR INFO .
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-dir " \fIDIR\fR"
Directory for log files. Default:
.BR logs .
.TP
.BR \-\-color ", " \-\-no\-color
Force colored output on or off.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_CONFIG
Config file to read when
.B \-\-config
is not given.
.TP
.BR MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_CLUSTER ", " MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_DISCOVERY_TIMEOUT ", " \
MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_LOG_LEVEL ", " MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_LOG_DIR ", " MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_COLOR
Override the corresponding config file key. Command line options win over
these.
.SH FILES
Searched in order; the first one that exists is used:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_CONFIG
./mu2edaq-commandline-tools.yaml
./config/mu2edaq-commandline-tools.yaml
<checkout>/config/mu2edaq-commandline-tools.yaml
~/.config/mu2edaq/commandline-tools.yaml
/etc/mu2edaq/commandline-tools.yaml
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The configuration could not be read.
.TP
.B 2
No command was given, or the command line was invalid.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show what the tools would use, from the current directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mu2edaq\-tools config
.fi
.RE
.PP
Point at a different cluster for one invocation:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mu2edaq\-tools \-\-cluster mu2edaq\-test config \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq-tools-info (1),
.BR mu2edaq-commandline-tools-bootstrap (1),
.BR mu2edaq_cli_core (3),
.BR mu2edaq_commandline_tools (3)
